## psc/token.pengu — modelo de tokens y tabla de palabras reservadas.
##
## `Token` es POD: no guarda strings. El lexema se obtiene del `SourceFile` con
## `token_span`; los literales usan tablas laterales indexadas por `aux`.
##
## ## Convenciones
## - `start` es inclusivo y `end` exclusivo, en bytes de `SourceFile.text`.
## - `line`/`col` son 1-indexed; `col` es columna de byte.
## - `kw` solo tiene sentido cuando `kind == TokKeyword`; en el resto vale
##   `KwNotKeyword`.
##
## ## Por qué los prefijos `Tok`/`Kw`
## Los nombres de variantes de un `omen` son globales en todo el programa. Un
## `omen` con variantes `Error`, `None` o `Read` colisiona con la stdlib. Los
## prefijos `Tok*`, `Kw*`, `Lex*`, `Com*`, `Seg*` y `Src*` evitan esas
## colisiones sin perder legibilidad.
##
## ## Memoria
## `Token`, `KeywordEntry` y `ByteSpan` son valores puros. `KeywordTable` es
## dueña de su lista; las palabras son literales estáticos.

import psc.span as pspan

## Categoría léxica de un token.
##
## Los keywords no tienen una variante por palabra: usan `TokKeyword` y
## `Token.kw`. Así este enum queda pequeño y el parser compara `tok.kw`.
omen TokenKind:
    ## Fin de archivo.
    TokEof
    ## Salto de línea significativo; puede cubrir varias líneas en blanco.
    TokNewline
    ## Apertura de bloque.
    TokIndent
    ## Cierre de bloque.
    TokDedent

    ## Identificador ASCII.
    TokIdentifier
    ## Palabra reservada; el valor exacto está en `Token.kw`.
    TokKeyword
    ## Entero decimal/hex/bin/oct.
    TokIntLit
    ## Flotante.
    TokFloatLit
    ## String normal, raw o triple.
    TokStringLit
    ## Char literal.
    TokCharLit
    ## Cuerpo C de un `antiquus`.
    TokAntiquusBody
    ## Token de recuperación; el parser puede saltarlo.
    TokError

    ## `(`
    TokLeftParen
    ## `)`
    TokRightParen
    ## `[`
    TokLeftBracket
    ## `]`
    TokRightBracket
    ## `{`
    TokLeftBrace
    ## `}`
    TokRightBrace

    ## `,`
    TokComma
    ## `:`
    TokColon
    ## `;`
    TokSemicolon
    ## `.`
    TokDot
    ## `..`
    TokDotDot
    ## `...`
    TokEllipsis
    ## `->`
    TokArrow
    ## `@`
    TokAt

    ## `+`
    TokPlus
    ## `-`
    TokMinus
    ## `*`
    TokStar
    ## `/`
    TokSlash
    ## `%`
    TokPercent
    ## `&`
    TokAmpersand
    ## `|`
    TokVerticalBar
    ## `^`
    TokCaret
    ## `~`
    TokTilde
    ## `!` (solo aparece suelto en `!=`; suelto lo rechaza el parser)
    TokBang

    ## `=`
    TokAssign
    ## `==`
    TokEqual
    ## `!=`
    TokNotEqual
    ## `<`
    TokLess
    ## `<=`
    TokLessOrEqual
    ## `>`
    TokGreater
    ## `>=`
    TokGreaterOrEqual
    ## `<<`
    TokShiftLeft
    ## `>>`
    TokShiftRight

    ## `+=`
    TokPlusAssign
    ## `-=`
    TokMinusAssign
    ## `*=`
    TokStarAssign
    ## `/=`
    TokSlashAssign
    ## `%=`
    TokPercentAssign
    ## `&=`
    TokAmpersandAssign
    ## `|=`
    TokVerticalBarAssign
    ## `^=`
    TokCaretAssign
    ## `<<=`
    TokShiftLeftAssign
    ## `>>=`
    TokShiftRightAssign

## Palabra reservada. `KwNotKeyword` es el valor por defecto.
##
## Las palabras *soft* (`self`, `unsafe`, `over`, `frozen`, `inline`, `ritual`,
## `do`, `type`, `size`, `main`, `ok`, `err`) no están aquí: el lexer las emite
## como `TokIdentifier` y el parser las interpreta por contexto.
omen KeywordKind:
    ## El token no es un keyword.
    KwNotKeyword

    ## `alias`
    KwAlias
    ## `and`
    KwAnd
    ## `antiquus`
    KwAntiquus
    ## `as`
    KwAs
    ## `banish`
    KwBanish
    ## `bind`
    KwBind
    ## `break`
    KwBreak
    ## `bytes`
    KwBytes
    ## `calling`
    KwCalling
    ## `chr`
    KwChr
    ## `concept`
    KwConcept
    ## `const`
    KwConst
    ## `continue`
    KwContinue
    ## `cyclus`
    KwCyclus
    ## `declare`
    KwDeclare
    ## `defer`
    KwDefer
    ## `defined`
    KwDefined
    ## `derive`
    KwDerive
    ## `donum`
    KwDonum
    ## `echo`
    KwEcho
    ## `else`
    KwElse
    ## `enchanting`
    KwEnchanting
    ## `errdefer`
    KwErrdefer
    ## `error`
    KwError
    ## `essence`
    KwEssence
    ## `false`
    KwFalse
    ## `for`
    KwFor
    ## `from`
    KwFrom
    ## `if`
    KwIf
    ## `import`
    KwImport
    ## `in`
    KwIn
    ## `include`
    KwInclude
    ## `insignia`
    KwInsignia
    ## `into`
    KwInto
    ## `is`
    KwIs
    ## `judge`
    KwJudge
    ## `lambda`
    KwLambda
    ## `ldflag`
    KwLdflag
    ## `let`
    KwLet
    ## `link`
    KwLink
    ## `many`
    KwMany
    ## `maybe`
    KwMaybe
    ## `none`
    KwNone
    ## `not`
    KwNot
    ## `null`
    KwNull
    ## `of`
    KwOf
    ## `omen`
    KwOmen
    ## `or`
    KwOr
    ## `ord`
    KwOrd
    ## `return`
    KwReturn
    ## `rune`
    KwRune
    ## `seal`
    KwSeal
    ## `set`
    KwSet
    ## `shard`
    KwShard
    ## `sigil`
    KwSigil
    ## `some`
    KwSome
    ## `static`
    KwStatic
    ## `step`
    KwStep
    ## `test`
    KwTest
    ## `to`
    KwTo
    ## `transmute`
    KwTransmute
    ## `true`
    KwTrue
    ## `try`
    KwTry
    ## `unless`
    KwUnless
    ## `var`
    KwVar
    ## `weave`
    KwWeave
    ## `when`
    KwWhen
    ## `where`
    KwWhere
    ## `while`
    KwWhile
    ## `with`
    KwWith

    ## `type of` (token compuesto)
    KwTypeOf
    ## `size of` (token compuesto)
    KwSizeOf

## Un token léxico.
##
## ## Memoria
## Valor puro: no tiene heap.
rune Token derive Par:
    ## Categoría.
    kind as TokenKind
    ## Keyword exacto cuando `kind == TokKeyword`; `KwNotKeyword` si no.
    kw as KeywordKind
    ## Offset inclusivo.
    start as int
    ## Offset exclusivo.
    end as int
    ## Línea 1-indexed del primer byte.
    line as int
    ## Columna de byte 1-indexed del primer byte.
    col as int
    ## Payload auxiliar; ver la tabla del contrato en `lexer_state.pengu`.
    aux as int

## Una entrada de la tabla de keywords.
rune KeywordEntry derive Par:
    ## Lexema en minúsculas.
    word as string
    ## Keyword asociado.
    kind as KeywordKind
    ## Primer byte del lexema (para descartar rápido).
    first as int
    ## Longitud del lexema.
    len as int

## Tabla de palabras reservadas.
##
## La búsqueda es lineal: 70 comparaciones de igualdad por identificador es
## barato en C y evita depender del orden lexicográfico de `string` (que el
## lenguaje no ofrece). Si el benchmark lo justifica, se añade un índice.
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish table` libera `entries`; los `word` son literales estáticos.
rune KeywordTable derive Nexus:
    ## Entradas ordenadas alfabéticamente.
    entries as list of KeywordEntry

## Añade una entrada a la tabla calculando `first` y `len`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Hace `push`; la palabra es un literal estático.
weave add_keyword with t as ref to KeywordTable, word as string, k as KeywordKind into void:
    var raw as ref to frozen byte is bytes of word
    var first as int is 0
    if word length > 0:
        set first is (raw at 0) to int
    var e as KeywordEntry is with word is word, kind is k, first is first, len is (word length)
    calling t->entries.push with e

## Construye la tabla de keywords completa.
##
## ## Memoria
## Asigna una lista; liberar con `banish`.
weave keyword_table_new into KeywordTable:
    var t as KeywordTable is with entries is list of KeywordEntry
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "alias", KwAlias
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "and", KwAnd
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "antiquus", KwAntiquus
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "as", KwAs
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "banish", KwBanish
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "bind", KwBind
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "break", KwBreak
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "bytes", KwBytes
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "calling", KwCalling
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "chr", KwChr
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "concept", KwConcept
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "const", KwConst
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "continue", KwContinue
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "cyclus", KwCyclus
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "declare", KwDeclare
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "defer", KwDefer
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "defined", KwDefined
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "derive", KwDerive
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "donum", KwDonum
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "echo", KwEcho
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "else", KwElse
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "enchanting", KwEnchanting
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "errdefer", KwErrdefer
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "error", KwError
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "essence", KwEssence
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "false", KwFalse
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "for", KwFor
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "from", KwFrom
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "if", KwIf
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "import", KwImport
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "in", KwIn
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "include", KwInclude
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "insignia", KwInsignia
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "into", KwInto
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "is", KwIs
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "judge", KwJudge
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "lambda", KwLambda
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "ldflag", KwLdflag
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "let", KwLet
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "link", KwLink
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "many", KwMany
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "maybe", KwMaybe
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "none", KwNone
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "not", KwNot
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "null", KwNull
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "of", KwOf
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "omen", KwOmen
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "or", KwOr
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "ord", KwOrd
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "return", KwReturn
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "rune", KwRune
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "seal", KwSeal
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "set", KwSet
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "shard", KwShard
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "sigil", KwSigil
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "some", KwSome
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "static", KwStatic
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "step", KwStep
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "test", KwTest
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "to", KwTo
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "transmute", KwTransmute
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "true", KwTrue
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "try", KwTry
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "unless", KwUnless
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "var", KwVar
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "weave", KwWeave
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "when", KwWhen
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "where", KwWhere
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "while", KwWhile
    calling add_keyword with sigil of t, "with", KwWith
    return t

## Busca un keyword con búsqueda binaria.
##
## ## Retorno
## `KwNotKeyword` si `word` no es una palabra reservada dura.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(log n), no asigna.
weave keyword_lookup with t as ref to KeywordTable, word as string into KeywordKind:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < t->entries.len:
        var e as KeywordEntry is t->entries at i
        if word == e.word:
            return e.kind
        set i is i + 1
    return KwNotKeyword

## Devuelve el lexema de un keyword, o `""` si no está en la tabla.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un literal estático; no liberar.
weave keyword_name with t as ref to KeywordTable, k as KeywordKind into string:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < t->entries.len:
        var e as KeywordEntry is t->entries at i
        if e.kind == k:
            return e.word
        set i is i + 1
    return ""

## Nombre estable de una categoría de token.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un literal estático; no liberar.
weave token_kind_name with k as TokenKind into string:
    return judge k:
        when TokEof -> "Eof"
        when TokNewline -> "Newline"
        when TokIndent -> "Indent"
        when TokDedent -> "Dedent"
        when TokIdentifier -> "Identifier"
        when TokKeyword -> "Keyword"
        when TokIntLit -> "IntLit"
        when TokFloatLit -> "FloatLit"
        when TokStringLit -> "StringLit"
        when TokCharLit -> "CharLit"
        when TokAntiquusBody -> "AntiquusBody"
        when TokError -> "Error"
        when TokLeftParen -> "LeftParen"
        when TokRightParen -> "RightParen"
        when TokLeftBracket -> "LeftBracket"
        when TokRightBracket -> "RightBracket"
        when TokLeftBrace -> "LeftBrace"
        when TokRightBrace -> "RightBrace"
        when TokComma -> "Comma"
        when TokColon -> "Colon"
        when TokSemicolon -> "Semicolon"
        when TokDot -> "Dot"
        when TokDotDot -> "DotDot"
        when TokEllipsis -> "Ellipsis"
        when TokArrow -> "Arrow"
        when TokAt -> "At"
        when TokPlus -> "Plus"
        when TokMinus -> "Minus"
        when TokStar -> "Star"
        when TokSlash -> "Slash"
        when TokPercent -> "Percent"
        when TokAmpersand -> "Ampersand"
        when TokVerticalBar -> "VerticalBar"
        when TokCaret -> "Caret"
        when TokTilde -> "Tilde"
        when TokBang -> "Bang"
        when TokAssign -> "Assign"
        when TokEqual -> "Equal"
        when TokNotEqual -> "NotEqual"
        when TokLess -> "Less"
        when TokLessOrEqual -> "LessOrEqual"
        when TokGreater -> "Greater"
        when TokGreaterOrEqual -> "GreaterOrEqual"
        when TokShiftLeft -> "ShiftLeft"
        when TokShiftRight -> "ShiftRight"
        when TokPlusAssign -> "PlusAssign"
        when TokMinusAssign -> "MinusAssign"
        when TokStarAssign -> "StarAssign"
        when TokSlashAssign -> "SlashAssign"
        when TokPercentAssign -> "PercentAssign"
        when TokAmpersandAssign -> "AmpersandAssign"
        when TokVerticalBarAssign -> "VerticalBarAssign"
        when TokCaretAssign -> "CaretAssign"
        when TokShiftLeftAssign -> "ShiftLeftAssign"
        when TokShiftRightAssign -> "ShiftRightAssign"

## Rango de bytes de un token.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave token_span with t as Token into pspan.ByteSpan:
    return with start is t.start, end is t.end

## `true` cuando el token es un keyword concreto.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave is_kw with t as Token, k as KeywordKind into bool:
    return t.kind == TokKeyword and t.kw == k
